issues/172 (was 171 #7) -- StopIteration.value read in an explicit handler goes through the single global exception slot (__pyc_exc__), which unions every StopIteration in the program (here "s", 7 and None), so the read is refused as {None, int64, str}. The CreationSets are already separated by value type; the confluence is the slot. Fixing it needs exception flow along the call graph (which raises reach which handler), not a coarser value type. CPython prints 1 then s, which the check file records.
